  "content": {
    "id": "p40-q19-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "19",
    "prompt": "A regular $n$-sided polygon is inscribed in a circle of radius $r$. The side length of the polygon is denoted by $s$, and the distance from the centre of the circle to any side of the polygon is denoted by $a$.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [
      {
        "id": "p40-q19-diagram",
        "role": "question",
        "format": "tikz",
        "code": "% mathsmap-diagram-colours {\"version\":1,\"kind\":\"geometry\",\"base\":[],\"semantic\":[],\"reference\":\"source page 40 p40-q19-diagram\"}\n\\begin{tikzpicture}[line width=0.8pt,every node/.style={font=\\fontsize{10}{12}\\selectfont,text=black}]\n\\special{dvisvgm:raw <metadata data-graph-strokes=\"1\"/>}\n\\coordinate (O) at (0,0);\n\\coordinate (V0) at (90:2);\n\\coordinate (V1) at (18:2);\n\\coordinate (V2) at (-54:2);\n\\coordinate (V3) at (-126:2);\n\\coordinate (V4) at (162:2);\n\\coordinate (M) at ($(V0)!0.5!(V1)$);\n\\draw[black] (O) circle (2);\n\\draw[black] (V0)--(V1)--(V2)--(V3)--(V4)--cycle;\n\\draw[black] (O)--node[midway,left] {$r$} (V0);\n\\draw[black] (O)--node[midway,below right] {$a$} (M);\n\\path (V0)--node[midway,above right] {$s$} (V1);\n\\end{tikzpicture}",
        "src": null,
        "widthMm": 65,
        "alt": "Mathematical diagram",
        "overlayOf": null,
        "transparent": false,
        "axes": null,
        "spec": {
          "sourcePage": 40,
          "sourceRegion": "Question 19, right column",
          "description": "A pentagon illustrates the general regular n-sided polygon. One vertex is at the top and the bottom side is horizontal. The radius, side and centre-to-side-midpoint segment are labelled r, s and a.",
          "mathematics": "All five illustrative vertices lie on the circle. The segment labelled a ends at the midpoint of the side labelled s and is perpendicular to that side. The illustration does not restrict n to 5.",
          "answerVisibility": "All supplied geometry and labels remain visible in the question."
        },
        "derived": false,
        "reviewStatus": "needs-review"
      }
    ],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p40-q19-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "Find an expression for $r$ in terms of $s$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$r=\\dfrac{s}{2\\sin(\\frac{\\pi}{n})}$.",
          "worked": "Join the centre to the endpoints of one side and bisect the resulting isosceles triangle. The right triangle has angle $\\frac{\\pi}{n}$, opposite side $\\frac{s}{2}$ and hypotenuse $r$.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\sin\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{n}\\right)&=\\frac{s}{2r}\\\\r&=\\frac{s}{2\\sin(\\pi/n)}.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 32
      },
      {
        "id": "p40-q19-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "Find an expression for $r$ in terms of $a$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$r=\\dfrac{a}{\\cos(\\frac{\\pi}{n})}$.",
          "worked": "In the same right triangle, the adjacent side is $a$ and the hypotenuse is $r$.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\cos\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{n}\\right)&=\\frac{a}{r}\\\\r&=\\frac{a}{\\cos(\\pi/n)}.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 26
      },
      {
        "id": "p40-q19-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "Show that the area $A_n$ of the polygon is given by\n$$A_n=\\frac12nr^2\\sin\\left(\\frac{2\\pi}{n}\\right).$$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$A_n=\\dfrac12nr^2\\sin(\\frac{2\\pi}{n})$.\n\nDivide the polygon into $n$ congruent triangles with two sides $r$ and included angle $\\frac{2\\pi}{n}$.",
          "worked": "Joining the centre to every vertex divides the polygon into $n$ congruent triangles. Each has two sides of length $r$ and included angle $\\frac{2\\pi}{n}$.\n$$\\begin{align*}A_n&=n\\left(\\frac12r\\cdot r\\sin\\left(\\frac{2\\pi}{n}\\right)\\right)\\\\A_n&=\\frac12nr^2\\sin\\left(\\frac{2\\pi}{n}\\right).\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 32
      },
      {
        "id": "p40-q19-d",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "d",
        "prompt": "Prove that $A_n$ approaches $\\pi r^2$ as $n$ approaches $\\infty$. Hint: Use your answer to the previous exercise.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$A_n\\to\\pi r^2$.\n\nWrite $A_n=\\pi r^2(\\frac{\\sin u}{u})$, where $u=\\frac{2\\pi}{n}$, and use $\\frac{\\sin u}{u}\\to1$ as $u\\to0$.",
          "worked": "Let $u=\\frac{2\\pi}{n}$.\n$$\\begin{align*}A_n&=\\frac12nr^2\\sin u\\\\A_n&=\\pi r^2\\frac{\\sin u}{u}.\\end{align*}$$\nAs $n\\to\\infty$, $u\\to0$. The previous exercise gives $\\frac{\\sin u}{u}\\to1$, so\n$$A_n\\to\\pi r^2.$$\nThus the polygon's area approaches the circle's area.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 40
      }
    ]
  },
